{"beat": 6, "name": "THE EXPRESS COMPANIES", "text": "Why didn't the post office carry heavier parcels? Ask the man who ran it. John Wanamaker, the Philadelphia merchant, was Postmaster General from 1889 to 1893. As The Cosmopolitan reported it in 1904, he said there were insuperable obstacles to the post office carrying parcels. First, the Adams Express Company. Then the American Express Company. Then Wells Fargo. Then the Southern Express Company. He was joking, and he wasn't. The express companies were a powerful lobby, and they liked the parcel business exactly as it was.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Why", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.16}, {"word": "didn't", "start": 0.16, "end": 0.3}, {"word": "the", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.48}, {"word": "post", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.72}, {"word": "office", "start": 0.72, "end": 1.04}, {"word": "carry", "start": 1.04, "end": 1.4}, {"word": "heavier", "start": 1.4, "end": 1.82}, {"word": "parcels?", "start": 1.82, "end": 2.44}, {"word": "Ask", "start": 3.02, "end": 3.24}, {"word": "the", "start": 3.24, "end": 3.46}, {"word": "man", "start": 3.46, "end": 3.66}, {"word": "who", "start": 3.66, "end": 3.84}, {"word": "ran", "start": 3.84, "end": 4.14}, {"word": "it.", "start": 4.14, "end": 4.32}, {"word": "John", "start": 4.84, "end": 5.18}, {"word": "Wanamaker,", "start": 5.18, "end": 5.92}, {"word": "the", "start": 6.3, "end": 6.44}, {"word": "Philadelphia", "start": 6.44, "end": 6.92}, {"word": "merchant,", "start": 6.92, "end": 7.46}, {"word": "was", "start": 7.96, "end": 8.18}, {"word": "Postmaster", "start": 8.18, "end": 8.88}, {"word": "General", "start": 8.88, "end": 9.38}, {"word": "from", "start": 9.38, "end": 9.64}, {"word": "1889", "start": 9.64, "end": 11.68}, {"word": "to", "start": 11.68, "end": 12.26}, {"word": "1893.", "start": 12.26, "end": 13.0}, {"word": "As", "start": 15.0, "end": 15.32}, {"word": "The", "start": 15.32, "end": 15.48}, {"word": "Cosmopolitan", "start": 15.48, "end": 16.32}, {"word"